WEBVTT FILE

1
00:06.075 --> 00:14.784
The grief of his wife's death... ...became greater and greater agony.

2
00:18.191 --> 00:24.028
The home they had so long shared together, became a tomb.

3
00:24.053 --> 00:28.581
A sweet memory of her joyous living.

4
00:28.605 --> 00:32.051
The sky to which she had once looked,

5
00:32.075 --> 00:36.605
was now only a covering for her dead body.

6
00:49.633 --> 00:53.840
The ever-beautiful flowers she had planted

7
00:53.864 --> 00:55.893
with her own hand,

8
00:55.918 --> 01:01.742
became nothing more than the lost roses of her cheeks.

9
01:05.655 --> 01:08.622
Confused by his great loss...

10
01:08.647 --> 01:11.195
the old man left that home,

11
01:11.219 --> 01:14.620
never to return again.

12
01:26.183 --> 01:29.349
At the funeral of the old man,

13
01:29.373 --> 01:31.743
unknown to his mourners,

14
01:31.768 --> 01:35.471
his dead wife was watching.

15
01:35.495 --> 01:39.099
First his wife, then he. - Tragic.

16
01:39.100 --> 01:41.379
Tell me something.

17
01:41.403 --> 01:45.384
Why was his wife buried in the ground and he sealed in a crypt?

18
01:45.408 --> 01:49.017
Something to do with family tradition. A superstition of some sort.

19
01:49.042 --> 01:54.368
Well, it's getting dark. We'd best be on our way.

20
01:57.024 --> 02:03.301
Then, as two of his mourners left his final resting place.

21
02:36.277 --> 02:42.165
Minutes later, the police, led by Inspector Daniel Clay, arrived at the scene.

22
02:42.190 --> 02:43.745
Who found him?

23
02:43.769 --> 02:45.391
The man and girl.

24
02:45.416 --> 02:48.389
Medical, uh, examiner been around yet?

25
02:48.469 --> 02:49.637
Just left.

26
02:49.662 --> 02:52.130
The morgue wagon ought to be along most any time.

27
02:52.155 --> 02:54.017
You get their statement?

28
02:54.042 --> 02:57.839
Yeah, much as we could. They're pretty scared.

29
02:57.864 --> 03:01.266
Finding a mess like this oughta make anyone frightened.

30
03:01.291 --> 03:05.564
Have one of the boys take the guy and the girl back to town.

31
03:05.591 --> 03:06.766
You take charge.

32
03:06.791 --> 03:08.785
Okay Inspector. What are you going to do?

33
03:08.810 --> 03:10.156
Look around a little.

34
03:10.180 --> 03:11.842
Pretty dark out there.

35
03:11.867 --> 03:15.649
Once you get beyond the range of those lights you won't be able to see your hand in front of your face.

36
03:15.674 --> 03:18.549
I will get one of the flashlights from the patrol car.

37
03:18.574 --> 03:19.656
You be careful, Clay.

38
03:19.686 --> 03:23.246
I'm a big boy now, Johnny.

39
04:18.114 --> 04:21.094
Looks like a bobcat tore into him.

40
04:21.118 --> 04:24.621
Yeah.

41
04:26.125 --> 04:28.527
Say Lieutenant,

42
04:28.528 --> 04:33.110
Do you get that funny odour? - How could I miss it?

43
04:33.134 --> 04:36.442
Oh, that'll be the morgue wagon now.

44
04:37.039 --> 04:40.356
That's the fifth siren in the last hour.

45
04:40.381 --> 04:45.827
Oh, something's happened down at the cemetery. A lot of police cars and lights. I stopped but I didn't see anything.

46
04:45.851 --> 04:51.788
Oh well, whatever it is, the morning paper will carry the whole story.

47
04:56.466 --> 04:59.646
You seem to still be up there somewhere.

48
04:59.670 --> 05:02.072
Maybe I am.

49
05:02.073 --> 05:06.557
I don't think I've ever seen you in this mood before.

50
05:06.582 --> 05:12.293
I guess it's because I've never been in this mood before.

51
05:15.591 --> 05:18.594
Something about your flight?

52
05:18.595 --> 05:21.758
Yeah.

53
05:21.783 --> 05:25.090
What happened, Jeff?

54
05:30.511 --> 05:32.846
I saw a flying saucer.

55
05:32.870 --> 05:34.115
A saucer?

56
05:34.116 --> 05:37.113
You mean the kind from up there?

57
05:37.137 --> 05:39.500
Yeah, or its counterpart.

58
05:39.524 --> 05:43.742
I was shaped like a huge cigar. Dan Eder saw it too.

59
05:43.767 --> 05:47.843
When it passed over, the whole compartment lighted up with a blinding glare.

60
05:47.868 --> 05:51.357
Then there was a tremendous wind that practically knocked us off our course.

61
05:51.382 --> 05:52.510
Well, did you report it?

62
05:52.535 --> 05:56.844
Yeah, radioed in immediately and they said well keep it quiet until you land.

63
05:56.869 --> 05:58.436
Then as soon as we landed...

64
05:58.461 --> 06:03.131
Big army brass grabbed us and made us swear to secrecy about the whole thing.

65
06:03.155 --> 06:04.739
Oh, it burns me up.

66
06:04.764 --> 06:07.612
These things have been seen for years. They're here, it's a fact.

67
06:07.637 --> 06:09.361
And the public ought to know about it.

68
06:09.385 --> 06:11.749
There must be something more you can do about it.

69
06:11.774 --> 06:15.849
Oh no there isn't. Oh, but what's the point of making a fuss.

70
06:15.873 --> 06:20.976
Last night I saw a flying object that couldn't possibly have been from this planet.

71
06:21.001 --> 06:22.569
But I can't say a word.

72
06:22.593 --> 06:24.573
I'm muzzled by army brass.

73
06:24.598 --> 06:28.453
I can't even admit I saw the thing.

74
08:29.252 --> 08:33.305
Sounds like Clay's in trouble.

75
08:39.944 --> 08:44.940
I bet that apparition we saw had something to do with it. Come on.

76
09:07.003 --> 09:08.481
Is he dead?

77
09:08.505 --> 09:10.759
Yeah.

78
09:10.784 --> 09:14.642
He's messed up as bad as those two back there.

79
09:14.667 --> 09:18.995
Do you suppose that saucer or whatever it was had something to do with this?

80
09:19.019 --> 09:21.999
Your guess is as good as mine, Larry.

81
09:22.023 --> 09:23.727
But one thing's sure.

82
09:23.751 --> 09:25.804
Inspector Clay is dead...

83
09:25.828 --> 09:27.467
...murdered...

84
09:27.491 --> 09:30.511
and somebody's responsible.

85
09:30.535 --> 09:32.613
You're in charge now, Lieutenant.

86
09:32.637 --> 09:34.823
Yeah, guess I am.

87
09:34.847 --> 09:36.642
Kelton. Yes Sir?

88
09:36.643 --> 09:38.843
Get back up to the car and get on the radio.

89
09:38.868 --> 09:41.216
Tell the coroner he's got to make another trip out here.

90
09:41.241 --> 09:42.881
Well, how about the lab boys?

91
09:42.906 --> 09:46.500
Who do you think we left back at the car, boy scouts?

92
09:46.525 --> 09:50.514
Come on, Larry.